IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`
IMPORT `sg-definitions`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation: Part 3 Division 2, ss 41 to 42A (contracts made before incorporation, the form of contracts, deeds, the common seal and the official seal, a company with a charitable purpose).
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively). s 42 is shown "[Repealed by Act 5 of 2004]" and is not encoded (NOTES.md, coverage table).
-- What the law of another country, the Charities Act 1994 or the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018 provides is not a source: it is a fact the caller supplies.
-- Answers: JUST TRUE (the test is met), JUST FALSE (the text says no in its own words), NOTHING (the text does not say). See the header of sgi-capacity.l4.

§ `Section 41(1) and (2): contracts made before incorporation`

-- (1): "Any contract or other transaction purporting to be entered into by a company prior to its formation or by any person on behalf of a company prior to its formation may be ratified by the company after its formation and thereupon the company becomes bound by and entitled to the benefit thereof as if it had been in existence at the date of the contract or other transaction and had been a party thereto."
-- src:5938 | 41.—(1) Any contract or other transaction purporting to be entered
-- src:5939 | into by a company prior to its formation or by any person on behalf of
-- src:5940 | a company prior to its formation may be ratified by the company after
-- src:5941 | its formation and thereupon the company becomes bound by and
-- src:5942 | entitled to the benefit thereof as if it had been in existence at the date
-- src:5943 | of the contract or other transaction and had been a party thereto.
@ref s 41(1) (src:5938-5943)
GIVEN `the contract or transaction purports to be entered into by the company prior to its formation or by a person on behalf of the company prior to its formation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has been formed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 41(1) the contract or transaction may be ratified by the company` MEANS
    IF `the contract or transaction purports to be entered into by the company prior to its formation or by a person on behalf of the company prior to its formation` AND `the company has been formed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any contract or other transaction purporting to be entered into ... prior to its formation ... may be ratified by the company after its formation" -- a permission whose conditions are not met; the text names no outcome (fork line F-I2)

-- src:5938 | 41.—(1) Any contract or other transaction purporting to be entered
-- src:5939 | into by a company prior to its formation or by any person on behalf of
-- src:5940 | a company prior to its formation may be ratified by the company after
-- src:5941 | its formation and thereupon the company becomes bound by and
-- src:5942 | entitled to the benefit thereof as if it had been in existence at the date
-- src:5943 | of the contract or other transaction and had been a party thereto.
@ref s 41(1) (src:5938-5943)
GIVEN `the contract or transaction purports to be entered into by the company prior to its formation or by a person on behalf of the company prior to its formation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has ratified it after its formation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 41(1) the company is bound by and entitled to the benefit of the contract or transaction` MEANS
    IF `the contract or transaction purports to be entered into by the company prior to its formation or by a person on behalf of the company prior to its formation` AND `the company has ratified it after its formation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may be ratified by the company after its formation and thereupon the company becomes bound by and entitled to the benefit thereof" (a status gated by "thereupon": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, items (b) and (c); fork line F-I11)

-- (2): "Prior to ratification by the company the person or persons who purported to act in the name or on behalf of the company are, in the absence of express agreement to the contrary, personally bound by the contract or other transaction and entitled to the benefit thereof."
-- "In the absence of express agreement to the contrary": once there is one, the text is silent (NOTHING; fork line F-I18). After ratification the subsection no longer speaks: NOTHING, not JUST FALSE, because the end of the period is an event and not a stated period, and subsection (1) does not say the person is released (fork line F-I30).
-- src:5945 | (2) Prior to ratification by the company the person or persons who
-- src:5946 | purported to act in the name or on behalf of the company are, in the
-- src:5947 | absence of express agreement to the contrary, personally bound by the
-- src:5948 | contract or other transaction and entitled to the benefit thereof.
@ref s 41(2) (src:5945-5948)
GIVEN `the person purported to act in the name or on behalf of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has ratified the contract or transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is express agreement to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 41(2) the person is personally bound by the contract or transaction and entitled to the benefit of it` MEANS
    IF `the person purported to act in the name or on behalf of the company` AND (NOT `the company has ratified the contract or transaction`)
    THEN (IF `there is express agreement to the contrary`
          THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "in the absence of express agreement to the contrary" is met; the text then says nothing of whether the person is bound (fork line F-I18)
          ELSE JUST TRUE)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Prior to ratification by the company the person or persons who purported to act in the name or on behalf of the company" -- another person, or the time after ratification, is outside the subsection (fork line F-I30)

§ `Section 41(3) to (9): the form of contracts, authentication, deeds and seals`

DECLARE `s 41(3) contract form` IS ONE OF
    `s 41(3)(a) a contract which if made between private persons would by law be required to be in writing under seal`
    `s 41(3)(b) a contract which if made between private persons would by law be required to be in writing signed by the parties to be charged`
    `s 41(3)(c) a contract which if made between private persons would by law be valid although made by parol only`
    `s 41(3) another contract`

DECLARE `s 41(3) way of making` IS ONE OF
    `s 41(3)(a) in writing under the common seal of the corporation`
    `s 41(3)(b) in writing signed by a person acting under the authority, express or implied, of the corporation`
    `s 41(3)(c) by parol by a person acting under the authority, express or implied, of the corporation`
    `s 41(3) another way`

-- (3): "Contracts on behalf of a corporation may be made as follows: (a) a contract which if made between private persons would by law be required to be in writing under seal may be made on behalf of the corporation in writing under the common seal of the corporation;
-- (b) a contract which ... would by law be required to be in writing signed by the parties to be charged therewith may be made on behalf of the corporation in writing signed by any person acting under its authority, express or implied;
-- (c) a contract which ... would by law be valid although made by parol only (and not reduced into writing) may be made by parol on behalf of the corporation by any person acting under its authority, express or implied".
-- A list of permitted ways, not closed with "only": a way the paragraphs do not pair with the contract's form is not addressed (NOTHING).
-- src:5952 | (3) Contracts on behalf of a corporation may be made as follows:
-- src:5954 | (a) a contract which if made between private persons would by
-- src:5955 | law be required to be in writing under seal may be made on
-- src:5956 | behalf of the corporation in writing under the common seal
-- src:5957 | of the corporation;
-- src:5959 | (b) a contract which if made between private persons would by
-- src:5960 | law be required to be in writing signed by the parties to be
-- src:5961 | charged therewith may be made on behalf of the
-- src:5962 | corporation in writing signed by any person acting under
-- src:5963 | its authority, express or implied;
-- src:5965 | (c) a contract which if made between private persons would by
-- src:5966 | law be valid although made by parol only (and not reduced
-- src:5967 | into writing) may be made by parol on behalf of the
-- src:5968 | corporation by any person acting under its authority,
-- src:5969 | express or implied,
-- src:5974 | and any contract so made is effectual in law and binds the corporation
-- src:5975 | and its successors and all other parties thereto and may be varied or
-- src:5976 | discharged in the manner in which it is authorised to be made.
@ref s 41(3) (src:5952-5976)
GIVEN form IS A `s 41(3) contract form`
      way IS A `s 41(3) way of making`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 41(3) the contract may be made on behalf of the corporation in the way` MEANS
    CONSIDER form
    WHEN `s 41(3)(a) a contract which if made between private persons would by law be required to be in writing under seal` THEN (IF way EQUALS `s 41(3)(a) in writing under the common seal of the corporation` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING)
    WHEN `s 41(3)(b) a contract which if made between private persons would by law be required to be in writing signed by the parties to be charged` THEN (IF way EQUALS `s 41(3)(b) in writing signed by a person acting under the authority, express or implied, of the corporation` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING)
    WHEN `s 41(3)(c) a contract which if made between private persons would by law be valid although made by parol only` THEN (IF way EQUALS `s 41(3)(c) by parol by a person acting under the authority, express or implied, of the corporation` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING)
    OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Contracts on behalf of a corporation may be made as follows: (a) ...; (b) ...; (c) ..." -- a contract of another form, or a way the paragraphs do not pair with it, is not addressed (fork line F-I2)

-- (3), last limb: "and any contract so made is effectual in law and binds the corporation and its successors and all other parties thereto and may be varied or discharged in the manner in which it is authorised to be made."
-- src:5974 | and any contract so made is effectual in law and binds the corporation
-- src:5975 | and its successors and all other parties thereto and may be varied or
-- src:5976 | discharged in the manner in which it is authorised to be made.
@ref s 41(3) (src:5974-5976)
GIVEN `the contract was made as paragraph (a), (b) or (c) provides` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 41(3) the contract is effectual in law and binds the corporation and its successors and all other parties` MEANS
    IF `the contract was made as paragraph (a), (b) or (c) provides`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any contract so made is effectual in law and binds ..." -- a contract not so made is outside the sentence

-- src:5974 | and any contract so made is effectual in law and binds the corporation
-- src:5975 | and its successors and all other parties thereto and may be varied or
-- src:5976 | discharged in the manner in which it is authorised to be made.
@ref s 41(3) (src:5974-5976)
GIVEN `the contract was made as paragraph (a), (b) or (c) provides` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the variation or discharge is made in the manner in which the contract is authorised to be made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 41(3) the contract may be varied or discharged` MEANS
    IF `the contract was made as paragraph (a), (b) or (c) provides` AND `the variation or discharge is made in the manner in which the contract is authorised to be made`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may be varied or discharged in the manner in which it is authorised to be made" -- a permission whose conditions are not met; the text names no outcome (fork line F-I2)

-- (4): "A document or proceeding requiring authentication by a corporation may be signed by an authorised officer of the corporation and need not be under its common seal."
-- src:5980 | (4) A document or proceeding requiring authentication by a
-- src:5981 | corporation may be signed by an authorised officer of the
-- src:5982 | corporation and need not be under its common seal.
@ref s 41(4) (src:5980-5982)
GIVEN `the document or proceeding requires authentication by a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document or proceeding is signed by an authorised officer of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 41(4) the document or proceeding may be signed by an authorised officer of the corporation` MEANS
    IF `the document or proceeding requires authentication by a corporation` AND `the document or proceeding is signed by an authorised officer of the corporation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A document or proceeding requiring authentication by a corporation may be signed by an authorised officer" -- a permission whose conditions are not met; the text names no outcome (fork line F-I2)

-- src:5980 | (4) A document or proceeding requiring authentication by a
-- src:5981 | corporation may be signed by an authorised officer of the
-- src:5982 | corporation and need not be under its common seal.
@ref s 41(4) (src:5980-5982)
GIVEN `the document or proceeding requires authentication by a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 41(4) the document or proceeding needs to be under the common seal` MEANS
    IF `the document or proceeding requires authentication by a corporation`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A document or proceeding requiring authentication by a corporation ... need not be under its common seal."
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of "a document or proceeding requiring authentication by a corporation"

-- (5): "A corporation may by writing under its common seal empower any person, either generally or in respect of any specified matters, as its agent or attorney to execute deeds on its behalf and a deed signed by such an agent or attorney on behalf of the corporation and under his or her seal,
-- or, subject to subsection (7), under the appropriate official seal of the corporation binds the corporation and has the same effect as if it were under its common seal."
-- src:5986 | (5) A corporation may by writing under its common seal empower
-- src:5987 | any person, either generally or in respect of any specified matters, as
-- src:5988 | its agent or attorney to execute deeds on its behalf and a deed signed
-- src:5989 | by such an agent or attorney on behalf of the corporation and under
-- src:5990 | his or her seal, or, subject to subsection (7), under the appropriate
-- src:5991 | official seal of the corporation binds the corporation and has the same
-- src:5992 | effect as if it were under its common seal.
@ref s 41(5) (src:5986-5992)
GIVEN `the corporation empowers the person by writing under its common seal, either generally or in respect of specified matters, as its agent or attorney to execute deeds on its behalf` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 41(5) the corporation may empower the person as its agent or attorney to execute deeds on its behalf` MEANS
    IF `the corporation empowers the person by writing under its common seal, either generally or in respect of specified matters, as its agent or attorney to execute deeds on its behalf`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A corporation may by writing under its common seal empower any person ... as its agent or attorney to execute deeds on its behalf" -- a permission whose method is not met; the text names no outcome (fork line F-I2)

-- src:5986 | (5) A corporation may by writing under its common seal empower
-- src:5987 | any person, either generally or in respect of any specified matters, as
-- src:5988 | its agent or attorney to execute deeds on its behalf and a deed signed
-- src:5989 | by such an agent or attorney on behalf of the corporation and under
-- src:5990 | his or her seal, or, subject to subsection (7), under the appropriate
-- src:5991 | official seal of the corporation binds the corporation and has the same
-- src:5992 | effect as if it were under its common seal.
@ref s 41(5) (src:5986-5992)
GIVEN `the person was empowered by writing under the common seal of the corporation as its agent or attorney to execute deeds` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the deed is signed by the agent or attorney on behalf of the corporation and under his or her seal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the deed is signed under the appropriate official seal of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the official seal is one subsection (7) allows` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 41(5) the deed binds the corporation and has the same effect as if it were under its common seal` MEANS
    IF    `the person was empowered by writing under the common seal of the corporation as its agent or attorney to execute deeds`
      AND (    `the deed is signed by the agent or attorney on behalf of the corporation and under his or her seal`
            OR (`the deed is signed under the appropriate official seal of the corporation` AND `the official seal is one subsection (7) allows`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a deed signed by such an agent or attorney on behalf of the corporation and under his or her seal, or, subject to subsection (7), under the appropriate official seal of the corporation binds the corporation" -- a deed not so signed is outside the sentence

-- (6): "The authority of any such agent or attorney continues, as between the corporation and any person dealing with him or her, during the period (if any) mentioned in the instrument conferring the authority, or if no period is therein mentioned then until notice of the revocation or determination of his or her authority has been given to the person dealing with him or her."
-- A period fixed by the instrument or by the notice: outside it, JUST FALSE (the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a); fork line F-I22).
-- src:5994 | (6) The authority of any such agent or attorney continues, as
-- src:5995 | between the corporation and any person dealing with him or her,
-- src:5996 | during the period (if any) mentioned in the instrument conferring the
-- src:5997 | authority, or if no period is therein mentioned then until notice of the
-- src:5998 | revocation or determination of his or her authority has been given to
-- src:5999 | the person dealing with him or her.
@ref s 41(6) (src:5994-5999)
GIVEN `the instrument conferring the authority mentions a period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the last day of the period the instrument mentions` IS A DATE
      `notice of the revocation or determination of the authority has been given to the person dealing with the agent or attorney` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the notice was given` IS A DATE
      `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 41(6) the authority of the agent or attorney continues as between the corporation and the person dealing with the agent or attorney` MEANS
    IF `the instrument conferring the authority mentions a period`
    THEN (IF `the date asked` AT MOST `the last day of the period the instrument mentions`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "continues ... during the period (if any) mentioned in the instrument conferring the authority" (a period the text fixes in its own words, outside it)
    ELSE (IF `notice of the revocation or determination of the authority has been given to the person dealing with the agent or attorney` AND `the date asked` AT LEAST `the day the notice was given`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if no period is therein mentioned then until notice of the revocation or determination of his or her authority has been given to the person dealing with him or her" (the notice has been given: the authority no longer continues as between them)
          ELSE JUST TRUE)

-- (7): "A corporation whose objects require or comprise the transaction of business outside Singapore may, if authorised by its constitution, have for use in any place outside Singapore an official seal, which must be a facsimile of the common seal of the corporation with the addition on its face of the name of the place where it is to be used
-- and the person affixing any such official seal must, in writing under his or her hand, certify on the instrument to which it is affixed the date on which and the place at which it is affixed."
-- src:6003 | (7) A corporation whose objects require or comprise the transaction
-- src:6004 | of business outside Singapore may, if authorised by its constitution,
-- src:6005 | have for use in any place outside Singapore an official seal, which
-- src:6006 | must be a facsimile of the common seal of the corporation with the
-- src:6007 | addition on its face of the name of the place where it is to be used and
-- src:6008 | the person affixing any such official seal must, in writing under his or
-- src:6009 | her hand, certify on the instrument to which it is affixed the date on
-- src:6010 | which and the place at which it is affixed.
@ref s 41(7) (src:6003-6010)
GIVEN `the corporation's objects require or comprise the transaction of business outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation is authorised by its constitution to have an official seal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 41(7) the corporation may have for use in a place outside Singapore an official seal` MEANS
    IF `the corporation's objects require or comprise the transaction of business outside Singapore` AND `the corporation is authorised by its constitution to have an official seal`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A corporation whose objects require or comprise the transaction of business outside Singapore may, if authorised by its constitution, have for use in any place outside Singapore an official seal" -- a permission whose conditions are not met; the text names no outcome (fork line F-I2)

-- src:6003 | (7) A corporation whose objects require or comprise the transaction
-- src:6004 | of business outside Singapore may, if authorised by its constitution,
-- src:6005 | have for use in any place outside Singapore an official seal, which
-- src:6006 | must be a facsimile of the common seal of the corporation with the
-- src:6007 | addition on its face of the name of the place where it is to be used and
-- src:6008 | the person affixing any such official seal must, in writing under his or
-- src:6009 | her hand, certify on the instrument to which it is affixed the date on
-- src:6010 | which and the place at which it is affixed.
@ref s 41(7) (src:6003-6010)
GIVEN `the official seal is a facsimile of the common seal of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the official seal has on its face the name of the place where it is to be used` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 41(7) the official seal is as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the official seal is a facsimile of the common seal of the corporation` AND `the official seal has on its face the name of the place where it is to be used`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an official seal, which must be a facsimile of the common seal of the corporation with the addition on its face of the name of the place where it is to be used" (a requirement: the provision's own question)

-- src:6003 | (7) A corporation whose objects require or comprise the transaction
-- src:6004 | of business outside Singapore may, if authorised by its constitution,
-- src:6005 | have for use in any place outside Singapore an official seal, which
-- src:6006 | must be a facsimile of the common seal of the corporation with the
-- src:6007 | addition on its face of the name of the place where it is to be used and
-- src:6008 | the person affixing any such official seal must, in writing under his or
-- src:6009 | her hand, certify on the instrument to which it is affixed the date on
-- src:6010 | which and the place at which it is affixed.
@ref s 41(7) (src:6003-6010)
GIVEN `the person affixing the official seal has certified in writing under his or her hand on the instrument the date on which it is affixed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person affixing the official seal has certified in writing under his or her hand on the instrument the place at which it is affixed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 41(7) the person affixing the official seal has certified the date and the place` MEANS
    IF `the person affixing the official seal has certified in writing under his or her hand on the instrument the date on which it is affixed` AND `the person affixing the official seal has certified in writing under his or her hand on the instrument the place at which it is affixed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection fixes no time for the certificate, so it does not say that a person who has not yet certified has failed (fork line F-I31)

DECLARE `s 41(7) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 41(7) certify in writing under his or her hand, on the instrument to which the official seal is affixed, the date on which and the place at which it is affixed`

-- The duty as a regulative rule. No time is fixed, so no trace reaches BREACH (listed in NOTES.md under "Rules with no breach path").
-- src:6003 | (7) A corporation whose objects require or comprise the transaction
-- src:6004 | of business outside Singapore may, if authorised by its constitution,
-- src:6005 | have for use in any place outside Singapore an official seal, which
-- src:6006 | must be a facsimile of the common seal of the corporation with the
-- src:6007 | addition on its face of the name of the place where it is to be used and
-- src:6008 | the person affixing any such official seal must, in writing under his or
-- src:6009 | her hand, certify on the instrument to which it is affixed the date on
-- src:6010 | which and the place at which it is affixed.
@ref s 41(7) (src:6003-6010)
GIVEN `the name of the person affixing the official seal` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 41(7) act`
`s 41(7) the person affixing the official seal must certify the date and the place` MEANS
    PARTY Individual `the name of the person affixing the official seal`
    MUST `s 41(7) certify in writing under his or her hand, on the instrument to which the official seal is affixed, the date on which and the place at which it is affixed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 41(7) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY Individual `the name of the person affixing the official seal` BECAUSE "the person affixing the official seal did not certify on the instrument the date on which and the place at which it was affixed" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)

-- (8): "The fact that a power of attorney or document of authorisation given to or in favour of the donee of the power or agent of a corporation is not under seal does not, if such power of attorney or document of authorisation is valid as a power of attorney or document of authorisation in accordance with the laws of the country under which such corporation is incorporated,
-- affect for any purpose intended to be effected in Singapore the validity or effect of any instrument under seal executed on behalf of that corporation by such donee of the power or agent, which is for all such purposes whatsoever as valid as if such authority had been under seal."
-- src:6020 | (8) The fact that a power of attorney or document of authorisation
-- src:6021 | given to or in favour of the donee of the power or agent of a
-- src:6022 | corporation is not under seal does not, if such power of attorney or
-- src:6023 | document of authorisation is valid as a power of attorney or document
-- src:6024 | of authorisation in accordance with the laws of the country under
-- src:6025 | which such corporation is incorporated, affect for any purpose
-- src:6026 | intended to be effected in Singapore the validity or effect of any
-- src:6027 | instrument under seal executed on behalf of that corporation by such
-- src:6028 | donee of the power or agent, which is for all such purposes
-- src:6029 | whatsoever as valid as if such authority had been under seal.
@ref s 41(8) (src:6020-6029)
GIVEN `the power of attorney or document of authorisation is not under seal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is valid as a power of attorney or document of authorisation in accordance with the laws of the country under which the corporation is incorporated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instrument under seal was executed on behalf of the corporation by the donee of the power or agent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose is intended to be effected in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 41(8) the instrument under seal is as valid as if the authority had been under seal` MEANS
    IF    `the power of attorney or document of authorisation is not under seal`
      AND `it is valid as a power of attorney or document of authorisation in accordance with the laws of the country under which the corporation is incorporated`
      AND `the instrument under seal was executed on behalf of the corporation by the donee of the power or agent`
      AND `the purpose is intended to be effected in Singapore`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "does not, if such power of attorney or document of authorisation is valid ... in accordance with the laws of the country under which such corporation is incorporated, affect for any purpose intended to be effected in Singapore the validity or effect of any instrument under seal" -- where the "if" or the purpose is not met the text names no outcome (fork line F-I2)

`s 41(9) the day 15 May 1987` MEANS Date 15 5 1987

-- (9): "Subsection (8) also applies to every instrument under seal executed before 15 May 1987 on behalf of any corporation by a donee of a power or an agent of that corporation whose authority was not under seal."
-- An instrument executed on or after 15 May 1987 is not reached by this extension (subsection (8) itself may still apply to it): NOTHING.
-- src:6031 | Retrospective application
-- src:6033 | (9) Subsection (8) also applies to every instrument under seal
-- src:6034 | executed before 15 May 1987 on behalf of any corporation by a donee
-- src:6035 | of a power or an agent of that corporation whose authority was not
-- src:6036 | under seal.
@ref s 41(9) (src:6031-6036)
GIVEN `the instrument under seal was executed on behalf of the corporation by a donee of a power or an agent whose authority was not under seal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the instrument was executed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 41(9) subsection (8) applies to the instrument` MEANS
    IF `the instrument under seal was executed on behalf of the corporation by a donee of a power or an agent whose authority was not under seal` AND `the day the instrument was executed` LESS THAN `s 41(9) the day 15 May 1987`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subsection (8) also applies to every instrument under seal executed before 15 May 1987" -- an instrument executed on or after that date is outside the extension; subsection (8) may still reach it by its own terms

§ `Sections 41A to 41C: the common seal and the execution of deeds`

-- 41A(1): "A company may have a common seal but need not have one."
-- src:6040 | 41A.—(1) A company may have a common seal but need not have
-- src:6041 | one.
@ref s 41A(1) (src:6040-6041)
GIVEN `the body is a company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 41A(1) the company may have a common seal` MEANS
    IF `the body is a company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A company may have a common seal" -- the subsection speaks of a company

-- src:6040 | 41A.—(1) A company may have a common seal but need not have
-- src:6041 | one.
@ref s 41A(1) (src:6040-6041)
GIVEN `the body is a company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 41A(1) the company needs to have a common seal` MEANS
    IF `the body is a company`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company may have a common seal but need not have one."
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of a company

-- 41A(2): "Sections 41B and 41C apply whether a company has a common seal or not." The answer does not depend on whether the company has a common seal.
-- src:6045 | (2) Sections 41B and 41C apply whether a company has a common
-- src:6046 | seal or not.
@ref s 41A(2) (src:6045-6046)
GIVEN `the body is a company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has a common seal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 41A(2) sections 41B and 41C apply to the company` MEANS
    IF `the body is a company`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- whether `the company has a common seal` is TRUE or FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Sections 41B and 41C apply whether a company has a common seal or not" -- the subsection speaks of a company

-- 41B(1): "A company may execute a document described or expressed as a deed without affixing a common seal onto the document by signature — (a) on behalf of the company by a director of the company and a secretary of the company; (b) on behalf of the company by at least 2 directors of the company; or (c) on behalf of the company by a director of the company in the presence of a witness who attests the signature."
-- src:6052 | 41B.—(1) A company may execute a document described or
-- src:6053 | expressed as a deed without affixing a common seal onto the
-- src:6054 | document by signature —
-- src:6056 | (a) on behalf of the company by a director of the company and
-- src:6057 | a secretary of the company;
-- src:6059 | (b) on behalf of the company by at least 2 directors of the
-- src:6060 | company; or
-- src:6065 | (c) on behalf of the company by a director of the company in
-- src:6066 | the presence of a witness who attests the signature.
@ref s 41B(1) (src:6052-6066)
GIVEN `the document is described or expressed as a deed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of directors of the company who sign on behalf of the company` IS A NUMBER
      `a secretary of the company signs on behalf of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a director of the company signs on behalf of the company in the presence of a witness who attests the signature` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 41B(1) the company may execute the document without affixing a common seal` MEANS
    IF    `the document is described or expressed as a deed`
      AND (    (`the number of directors of the company who sign on behalf of the company` AT LEAST 1 AND `a secretary of the company signs on behalf of the company`)
            OR `the number of directors of the company who sign on behalf of the company` AT LEAST 2
            OR `a director of the company signs on behalf of the company in the presence of a witness who attests the signature`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A company may execute a document described or expressed as a deed without affixing a common seal onto the document by signature — (a) ...; (b) ...; or (c) ..." -- a permission whose conditions are not met; the text names no outcome (fork line F-I2)

-- 41B(2): "A document mentioned in subsection (1) that is signed on behalf of the company in accordance with that subsection has the same effect as if the document were executed under the common seal of the company."
-- src:6070 | (2) A document mentioned in subsection (1) that is signed on behalf
-- src:6071 | of the company in accordance with that subsection has the same effect
-- src:6072 | as if the document were executed under the common seal of the
-- src:6073 | company.
@ref s 41B(2) (src:6070-6073)
GIVEN `the document is a document mentioned in subsection (1) and is signed on behalf of the company in accordance with that subsection` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 41B(2) the document has the same effect as if it were executed under the common seal of the company` MEANS
    IF `the document is a document mentioned in subsection (1) and is signed on behalf of the company in accordance with that subsection`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A document mentioned in subsection (1) that is signed on behalf of the company in accordance with that subsection has the same effect" -- another document is outside the subsection

-- 41B(3): "Where a document is to be signed by a person on behalf of more than one company, the document is not considered to be signed by that person for the purposes of subsection (1) or (2) unless the person signs the document separately in each capacity."
-- Once the person signs separately the "unless" is met and the text is silent (NOTHING; fork line F-I18).
-- src:6077 | (3) Where a document is to be signed by a person on behalf of more
-- src:6078 | than one company, the document is not considered to be signed by
-- src:6079 | that person for the purposes of subsection (1) or (2) unless the person
-- src:6080 | signs the document separately in each capacity.
@ref s 41B(3) (src:6077-6080)
GIVEN `the document is to be signed by the person on behalf of more than one company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person signs the document separately in each capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 41B(3) the document is considered to be signed by the person for the purposes of subsection (1) or (2)` MEANS
    IF `the document is to be signed by the person on behalf of more than one company`
    THEN (IF `the person signs the document separately in each capacity`
          THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "unless the person signs the document separately in each capacity" is met; the text then says nothing of whether the document is considered signed (fork line F-I18)
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the document is not considered to be signed by that person for the purposes of subsection (1) or (2) unless the person signs the document separately in each capacity"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a document is to be signed by a person on behalf of more than one company" -- a document signed for one company only is outside the subsection

-- 41B(4): "This section applies in the case of a document mentioned in subsection (1) that is executed by the company in the name or on behalf of another person, whether or not that person is also a company."
-- src:6084 | (4) This section applies in the case of a document mentioned in
-- src:6085 | subsection (1) that is executed by the company in the name or on
-- src:6086 | behalf of another person, whether or not that person is also a
-- src:6087 | company.
@ref s 41B(4) (src:6084-6087)
GIVEN `the document is a document mentioned in subsection (1) executed by the company in the name or on behalf of another person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 41B(4) section 41B applies to the document` MEANS
    IF `the document is a document mentioned in subsection (1) executed by the company in the name or on behalf of another person`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- whether or not that person is also a company
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section applies in the case of a document mentioned in subsection (1) that is executed by the company in the name or on behalf of another person" -- another document is outside the subsection

-- 41C: "Where any written law or rule of law requires any document to be under or executed under the common seal of a company, or provides for certain consequences if it is not, a document satisfies that written law or rule of law if the document is signed in the manner set out in section 41B(1)(a), (b) or (c) and (3)."
-- src:6091 | Alternative to sealing
-- src:6093 | 41C. Where any written law or rule of law requires any document
-- src:6094 | to be under or executed under the common seal of a company, or
-- src:6095 | provides for certain consequences if it is not, a document satisfies that
-- src:6096 | written law or rule of law if the document is signed in the manner set
-- src:6097 | out in section 41B(1)(a), (b) or (c) and (3).
@ref s 41C (src:6091-6097)
GIVEN `a written law or rule of law requires the document to be under or executed under the common seal of a company, or provides for certain consequences if it is not` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is signed in the manner set out in section 41B(1)(a), (b) or (c)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is signed in the manner set out in section 41B(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 41C the document satisfies the written law or rule of law` MEANS
    IF    `a written law or rule of law requires the document to be under or executed under the common seal of a company, or provides for certain consequences if it is not`
      AND `the document is signed in the manner set out in section 41B(1)(a), (b) or (c)`
      AND `the document is signed in the manner set out in section 41B(3)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a document satisfies that written law or rule of law if the document is signed in the manner set out in section 41B(1)(a), (b) or (c) and (3)" -- a sufficient condition, not stated with "only if"; where it is not met the text names no outcome (fork line F-I2)

§ `Section 42A: a company with a charitable purpose`

-- (1): "This section applies to a company or a foreign company — (a) that is registered under the Charities Act 1994; or (b) that has as its sole object or one of its principal objects a charitable purpose connected with persons, events or objects outside Singapore."
-- src:6107 | 42A.—(1) This section applies to a company or a foreign
-- src:6108 | company —
-- src:6110 | (a) that is registered under the Charities Act 1994; or
-- src:6112 | (b) that has as its sole object or one of its principal objects a
-- src:6113 | charitable purpose connected with persons, events or
-- src:6114 | objects outside Singapore.
@ref s 42A(1) (src:6107-6114)
GIVEN `the company or foreign company is registered under the Charities Act 1994` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company or foreign company has as its sole object or one of its principal objects a charitable purpose connected with persons, events or objects outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 42A(1) section 42A applies to the company or foreign company` MEANS
    IF `the company or foreign company is registered under the Charities Act 1994` OR `the company or foreign company has as its sole object or one of its principal objects a charitable purpose connected with persons, events or objects outside Singapore`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section applies to a company or a foreign company — (a) ...; or (b) ..." -- a body outside both paragraphs is not addressed; the subsection is not closed with "only"

-- (2): "A company or foreign company to which this section applies that is convicted of an offence under the Charities Act 1994 or any regulations made thereunder is deemed to be a company or foreign company (as the case may be) that is being used for purposes prejudicial to public welfare
-- and may be liable, in the case of a company, to be wound up by the Court under section 125(1)(n) of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018 or, in the case of a foreign company, to have its name struck off the register by the Registrar under section 377(8)."
