-- src:6121 | regulations made thereunder is deemed to be a company or foreign
-- src:6122 | company (as the case may be) that is being used for purposes
-- src:6123 | prejudicial to public welfare and may be liable, in the case of a
-- src:6124 | company, to be wound up by the Court under section 125(1)(n) of the
-- src:6125 | Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018 or, in the case of
-- src:6126 | a foreign company, to have its name struck off the register by the
-- src:6127 | Registrar under section 377(8).
@ref s 42A(2) (src:6119-6127)
GIVEN `section 42A applies to the company or foreign company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company or foreign company is convicted of an offence under the Charities Act 1994 or any regulations made thereunder` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 42A(2) the company or foreign company is deemed to be used for purposes prejudicial to public welfare` MEANS
    IF `section 42A applies to the company or foreign company` AND `the company or foreign company is convicted of an offence under the Charities Act 1994 or any regulations made thereunder`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A company or foreign company to which this section applies that is convicted of an offence under the Charities Act 1994 or any regulations made thereunder is deemed to be ... used for purposes prejudicial to public welfare" -- another body, or one not convicted, is outside the subsection

